  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Consider the finite region bounded by the curve $x=-8+6y-{y}^{2}$ and the $y$-axis. What integral gives the volume of the solid generated when that region is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis?",
  "worked_solution": "First, we determine the points where the curve intersects the $y$-axis by solving the following equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8+6y-{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-6y+8 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)(y-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $y=2$ and $y=4.$ So, we need to integrate from $y=2$ to $y=4.$\n\nUsing the shell method, the volume of the solid can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =2\\pi {\\int }_{c}^{d}yf(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{2}^{4}y(-8+6y-{y}^{2})\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$",
